========================================================================
  PART 1: A000255, COMPATIBLE PAIRS, AND THE OVERLAP PYRAMID
========================================================================

  A000255(n) — permutations with no succession:
    A000255(0) = 1
    A000255(1) = 1
    A000255(2) = 3
    A000255(3) = 11
    A000255(4) = 53
    A000255(5) = 309
    A000255(6) = 2119
    A000255(7) = 16687

  THM-215: #{compatible pairs (σ,τ)} = n! × A000255(n-1):
    n=3: 18 / 36 = 1/2 = 0.500000
    n=4: 264 / 576 = 11/24 = 0.458333
    n=5: 6360 / 14400 = 53/120 = 0.441667
    n=6: 222480 / 518400 = 103/240 = 0.429167
    n=7: 10679760 / 25401600 = 2119/5040 = 0.420437

  Asymptotic: compatible fraction → 1/e = 0.367879

========================================================================
  PART 2: THE OVERLAP PYRAMID f(n,a)
========================================================================


  f(n,a) = #{compatible ordered pairs with exactly a shared directed arcs}

  Properties (from repo):
    f(n, n-1) = n!  (only σ=τ has all n-1 arcs shared)
    f(n, n-2) = (n-1)·n!  (adjacent transpositions)
    Σ_a f(n,a) = n! × A000255(n-1)  (total compatible pairs)

  n=3: f(n,a) for a = 0..2
    f(3,0) =        0  (per σ: 0)
    f(3,1) =       12  (per σ: 2)
    f(3,2) =        6  (per σ: 1)
    Total: 18 (expected n!×A000255(n-1) = 18): ✓
    f(n,n-1)/n! = 1 (should be 1)
    f(n,n-2)/n! = 2 (should be n-1=2)
    f(n,0)/n! = 0

  n=4: f(n,a) for a = 0..3
    f(4,0) =       48  (per σ: 2)
    f(4,1) =      120  (per σ: 5)
    f(4,2) =       72  (per σ: 3)
    f(4,3) =       24  (per σ: 1)
    Total: 264 (expected n!×A000255(n-1) = 264): ✓
    f(n,n-1)/n! = 1 (should be 1)
    f(n,n-2)/n! = 3 (should be n-1=3)
    f(n,0)/n! = 2

  n=5: f(n,a) for a = 0..4
    f(5,0) =     1680  (per σ: 14)
    f(5,1) =     2400  (per σ: 20)
    f(5,2) =     1680  (per σ: 14)
    f(5,3) =      480  (per σ: 4)
    f(5,4) =      120  (per σ: 1)
    Total: 6360 (expected n!×A000255(n-1) = 6360): ✓
    f(n,n-1)/n! = 1 (should be 1)
    f(n,n-2)/n! = 4 (should be n-1=4)
    f(n,0)/n! = 14

  n=6: f(n,a) for a = 0..5
    f(6,0) =    64800  (per σ: 90)
    f(6,1) =    82800  (per σ: 115)
    f(6,2) =    51840  (per σ: 72)
    f(6,3) =    18720  (per σ: 26)
    f(6,4) =     3600  (per σ: 5)
    f(6,5) =      720  (per σ: 1)
    Total: 222480 (expected n!×A000255(n-1) = 222480): ✓
